│ - Credit card balances                                                                                                 │
│ - Unsecured personal loans                                                                                             │
│ - Any debt above roughly 7–9% APR                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                        │
│ Potentially maintain or pay more slowly on:                                                                            │
│ - Low-rate mortgage debt                                                                                               │
│ - Promotional financing if terms are clear and payoff timing is controlled                                             │
│ - Student or secured debt with comparatively low fixed rates                                                           │
│                                                                                                                        │
│ The key question is whether your cash is earning more than the debt is costing after tax and risk.                     │
│                                                                                                                        │
│ #### 4. Lower utilization if revolving debt is involved                                                                │
│ If part of your debt load is on credit cards, utilization management is critical for credit health.                    │
